# Repo-owned plugin boundary

- Treat this repository's plugin surface as a checked-in manifest plus explicit references to `rules`, `skills`, `.cursor/agents`, and `.cursor/hooks.json`.
- Keep shipped hooks and agents bounded to the files present in this repo and the validators that inspect them.
- Do not imply commands, marketplace publication, MCP defaults, custom modes, or background-agent provisioning unless matching artifacts and validators land in the same change.
- Keep local plugin instructions aligned with `docs/local-plugin-verification.md` and `~/.cursor/plugins/local` as a manual user-environment verification path.
- When plugin ownership claims change, update validator scripts and `docs/references.md` in the same edit.
